# qpepre inference comparison — legacy larger domain vs cleaned domain

All values are **qpepre in mm/h** (the loader un-log1p's the cleaned leg). Threshold metrics (CSI/FSS) are directly comparable across legs; per-pixel RMSE/CRPS are comparable in magnitude but the two grids cover different fields of view (legacy 224×128 ≈ +36% area vs cleaned 192×96) — footnote when reporting. CSI/FSS: higher is better; RMSE/CRPS: lower is better.

| leg | grid | encoding | RMSE_qpepre | CRPS_qpepre | CSI@0.1 | CSI@1.0 | CSI@5.0 | CSI@10.0 | CSI-P16 | FSS-P16 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| legacy_edm | 224×128 | raw mm/h | 1.1852 | 0.303335 | 0.244808 | 0.101699 | 0.009084 | 0.005044 | 0.0028 | 0.0089 |
| cleaned_edm | 192×96 | log1p(mm/h) | 0.9983 | 0.277011 | 0.504807 | 0.285894 | 0.081799 | 0.015071 | 0.0000 | 0.0009 |
| cleaned_flowcast | 192×96 | log1p(mm/h) | 0.9504 | 0.281942 | 0.482174 | 0.278795 | 0.086058 | 0.018670 | 0.0034 | 0.0081 |
| cleaned_bridge | 192×96 | log1p(mm/h) | 0.9757 | 0.328916 | 0.461301 | 0.206798 | 0.066121 | 0.025036 | 0.0029 | 0.0040 |
